diff --git a/docs/proxy-tls.md b/docs/proxy-tls.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5c5ba8e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/proxy-tls.md
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# Local TLS proxy candidate
+
+`deploy/nginx.conf.template` is a tested, loopback-only nginx candidate for the
+eight-enrolled-node profile in `head-and-enrollment-limits.md`. It is not a public
+deployment manifest. No collector, writer, API, frontend or efsn application code
+changes are needed for this proxy.
+
+The test uses Ubuntu nginx `1.24.0-2ubuntu7.18`, extracted without installing a
+service, and Node 22.11.0. Public hosting still requires a supported runtime and
+dependency review, operator-selected host/domain, certificate issuance/renewal,
+service supervision and final configuration acceptance.
+
+## Routes and trust boundary
+
+| Public HTTPS path | Destination |
+| --- | --- |
+| `/` and existing static files | Compiled `react-frontend/build` |
+| Exact `/api`, GET with WebSocket upgrade | Loopback collector reporter endpoint |
+| Exact `/stats-api/nodes`, `/blocks`, `/info`, `/charts` | Corresponding loopback API path, GET/HEAD only |
+| `/primus*`, `/external*`, other `/api*` and `/stats-api*` paths | 404 |
+
+The four API paths in the table all include the `/stats-api` prefix. The private
+snapshot writer uses direct loopback `/primus`. Keep the collector and API bound
+to numeric loopback; only the selected HTTPS listener is intended for public
+exposure after deployment review. No new HTTP redirect listener is included.
+
+The proxy discards incoming request headers before forwarding. On `/api`, it
+constructs only Host, Upgrade, Connection, the WebSocket key/version and three
+forwarding headers. `X-Forwarded-For` is the actual proxy TCP peer, not an incoming
+header chain. Tests supply all five header families understood by the installed
+`forwarded-for` package and verify the collector receives only the constructed
+values. Cookies and Authorization are not forwarded. Reporter credentials remain
+in the normal TLS-protected hello message.
+
+This assumes nginx directly receives client connections. Adding a CDN, load
+balancer or another proxy changes the address trust boundary and needs a reviewed
+trusted-proxy configuration and another acceptance run. Numeric IP metadata alone
+does not prove operator identity. Local processes remain inside the trust boundary.
+
+## Coordinated candidate limits
+
+| Boundary | Candidate |
+| --- | --- |
+| Collector identities / head / metadata | 8 / 65,536 bytes / 2,048 projected JSON bytes |
+| Collector incoming messages / pending writes | 4 MiB / 1 MiB per connection |
+| Snapshot message / node count | 1 MiB / 8 |
+| Collector TCP connections / hello deadline | 16 / 5 seconds |
+| nginx simultaneous reporter requests | 12, leaving collector room for the private writer |
+| nginx active requests / worker connections | 64 / 256 with one worker |
+| nginx HTTP request body / header buffers | 1 KiB / initial 1 KiB and two 8 KiB large buffers |
+| nginx header/body inactivity / keepalive / send inactivity | 5 / 15 / 10 seconds |
+| Upstream connect / API read / reporter read / reporter send inactivity | 2 / 5 / 45 / 10 seconds |
+| Snapshot interval / deadline used in the test | 250 / 2,000 milliseconds |
+| API snapshot/report validity used in the test | 10,000 / 30,000 milliseconds |
+
+Use the existing collector setting `COLLECTOR_MESSAGES_PER_SECOND=100` for this
+candidate. Writer/API intervals are fixture values, not selected public operating
+cadences. Process configurations still need to be coordinated in one reviewed
+manifest; the separate loaders do not cross-validate each other.
+
+nginx tunnels WebSocket bytes after upgrade. Its 1 KiB HTTP body cap does not limit
+WebSocket messages; the collector's 4 MiB cap does. Response buffering is disabled.
+Neither nginx's small buffers nor the collector write guard are a bound on total
+process, TLS or kernel memory. `limit_conn` counts requests with completed headers,
+not all partially opened sockets; worker connections also include upstream sockets.
+These settings are not a measured public-client capacity guarantee.
+
+Current efsn reports every 15 seconds and includes a node-ping exchange. The
+installed Primus closes clients silent for 35 seconds. nginx's 45-second upstream
+read inactivity allows the regular replies through. Missing hello closes at five
+seconds. API timeout returns 504; API stale data remains 503 with `no-store`.
+
+## Reproduction and remaining acceptance
+
+Render the template's explicit `@@RUN@@`, `@@TLS_PORT@@`, `@@HOST@@`, `@@CERT@@`,
+`@@KEY@@`, `@@BUILD@@`, `@@COLLECTOR_PORT@@` and `@@API_PORT@@` values into a private
+runtime directory. `@@BUILD@@` must point only at the compiled public directory.
+Validate with `nginx -t`; the test fixture renders and checks that exact template.
+Do not apply blanket environment substitution that expands nginx's `$variables`.
+The candidate deliberately listens on `127.0.0.1`; changing it is a deployment step.
+
+The opt-in test is `node --test test/proxy-tls.test.cjs`, with `TEST_NGINX`,
+`TEST_TLS_CA`, `TEST_TLS_CERT`, `TEST_TLS_KEY` and `DASHBOARD_PROXY_EVIDENCE` set.
+It expects Linux, the existing compiled frontend, a fresh evidence directory and
+a test certificate for `dashboard.test` and `127.0.0.1`. Its test CA is supplied
+only to individual clients; certificate verification stays enabled and no system
+trust store is changed. Never use the short-lived test certificates for hosting.
+
+This slice exercises real collector/writer/API code with an in-memory snapshot
+store and synthetic native-shaped reports. It serves and byte-compares compiled
+frontend assets, but does not execute a browser or run PostgreSQL or an efsn miner.
+Complete actual efsn WSS, PostgreSQL and browser integration and collector outage
+during mining before closing dashboard acceptance. Certificate renewal, service
+restart, log retention, public-network conditions and runtime/dependency review
+remain open. Access logs omit query strings and request bodies; production log
+ownership and rotation still need to be configured.
+
+Reference semantics: [nginx WebSocket tunneling](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/websocket.html),
+[proxy buffering, headers and timeouts](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_proxy_module.html),
+[connection accounting](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_limit_conn_module.html),
+[HTTP request limits](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_core_module.html),
+and [TLS settings](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_ssl_module.html).
